' Version 0.2 / 2026-10-29; Draft. Author/accountable: Solution Architect; consulted: Domain, Security, Accessibility, QA; reviewer: Engineering Lead; approver: Product Owner (pending); decision owner: Solution Architect. Assumptions ASM-001–012.
@startuml
' SEQ-01 Import; scope: workflow interaction; FR-IMP-001. SOURCE NOT RENDER-VALIDATED.
title SEQ-01 Import
actor Author
participant UI
participant API
participant Scanner
participant Worker
database Store
Author -> UI: Select file and import
UI -> API: Upload with scoped project
API -> Scanner: Validate type, size, malware
alt valid and safe
 Scanner -> Worker: Parse in isolated worker
 Worker -> Store: Stage canonical preview and warnings
 Worker --> UI: Report unsupported structures
 Author -> UI: Confirm import
 UI -> API: Commit reviewed import
 API -> Store: Create new revision idempotently
else rejected or failed
 Scanner --> UI: Actionable failure; source unchanged
end
legend right
Solid arrow = request; dashed arrow = response.
Authorization, audit and error handling are required at each relevant boundary.
endlegend
@enduml

@startuml
' SEQ-02 Save; scope: workflow interaction; FR-DOC-002. SOURCE NOT RENDER-VALIDATED.
title SEQ-02 Save
actor Author
participant Editor
participant API
database Store
Author -> Editor: Edit document
Editor -> Editor: Show unsaved / saving
Editor -> API: Save(expected revision, operation key)
API -> Store: Lock access epoch and current pointer; check permission
alt permission denied
 API --> Editor: Deny without disclosing receipt
else permission current
 API -> Store: Look up same actor, key and request receipt
 alt matching receipt exists
  Store --> API: Return original committed result
  API --> Editor: Acknowledge same revision
 else changed payload for key
  API --> Editor: Reject conflicting key reuse
 else new request
  API -> Store: Compare version; commit immutable revision, pointer, receipt and outbox
  alt committed durably
   Store --> API: Committed revision
   API --> Editor: Acknowledge revision
   Editor --> Author: Saved only if no newer local edits
  else stale or failed
   API --> Editor: Reject with recovery status
   Editor --> Author: Not saved; offer verified local recovery or copy
  end
 end
end
legend right
Solid arrow = request; dashed arrow = response.
Authorization, audit and error handling are required at each relevant boundary.
endlegend
@enduml

@startuml
' SEQ-03 Reconnect; scope: workflow interaction; FR-DOC-002, FR-IAM-002. SOURCE NOT RENDER-VALIDATED.
title SEQ-03 Reconnect
actor Author
participant Editor
participant API
database Store
Author -> Editor: Edit while disconnected
Editor --> Author: Not saved
Author -> Editor: Reconnect
Editor -> API: Request current revision and permission
API -> Store: Check grant and current revision
alt access revoked
 API --> Editor: Deny fresh read/write
else stale local edit
 API --> Editor: Return version conflict
 Editor --> Author: Review unsynced content if available; no automatic merge
else matching revision
 Editor -> API: Retry idempotent save
 API -> Store: Commit then acknowledge
end
legend right
Solid arrow = request; dashed arrow = response.
Authorization, audit and error handling are required at each relevant boundary.
endlegend
@enduml

@startuml
' SEQ-04 Restore; scope: workflow interaction; FR-DOC-003. SOURCE NOT RENDER-VALIDATED.
title SEQ-04 Restore
actor Author
participant UI
participant API
database Store
Author -> UI: Select older snapshot
UI -> API: Restore(snapshot, expected current revision)
API -> Store: Check authorization and expected version
alt current revision matches
 Store -> Store: Create new revision from snapshot
 Store --> UI: New revision; previous versions retained
else stale or unauthorized
 Store --> UI: Reject; no revision changed
end
legend right
Solid arrow = request; dashed arrow = response.
Authorization, audit and error handling are required at each relevant boundary.
endlegend
@enduml

@startuml
' SEQ-05 Export; scope: workflow interaction; FR-EXP-001, FR-FMT-001. SOURCE NOT RENDER-VALIDATED.
title SEQ-05 Export
actor Author
participant UI
participant API
queue Jobs
participant Worker
database Artifacts
Author -> UI: Export selected version
UI -> API: Authorized export with idempotency key
API -> Jobs: Queue frozen inputs and profile
Jobs -> Worker: Deliver job
Worker -> Worker: Validate and convert in isolation; stage per attempt
Worker -> Worker: Validate output and check current lease / fencing token
alt success and authorization current
 Worker -> Artifacts: Register artifact, hashes and report atomically
 Worker --> UI: Ready with scoped download
else failure
 Worker --> UI: Failure and retry option; prior artifact retained
end
legend right
Solid arrow = request; dashed arrow = response.
Authorization, audit and error handling are required at each relevant boundary.
endlegend
@enduml

@startuml
' SEQ-06 Submission to release; scope: workflow interaction; FR-PUB-001, FR-PUB-002, FR-RGT-001. SOURCE NOT RENDER-VALIDATED.
title SEQ-06 Submission to release
actor Author
actor Editor
participant API
participant Rights
participant Production
participant Catalog
Author -> API: Submit frozen revision and declarations
API -> Editor: Assign review
Editor -> API: Record decision with reason
alt revise or reject
 API --> Author: Notify decision; retain project
else accepted
 Editor -> Production: Prepare versioned rendition and proof
 Production -> API: Record artifact-specific approvals
 API -> Rights: Check current scoped grants and hold
 alt valid approvals and rights
  API -> Catalog: Release approved listing and event
 else missing or stale
  API --> Editor: Block release and show reason
 end
end
legend right
Solid arrow = request; dashed arrow = response.
Authorization, audit and error handling are required at each relevant boundary.
endlegend
@enduml

@startuml
' SEQ-07 Purchase; scope: workflow interaction; FR-COM-001. SOURCE NOT RENDER-VALIDATED.
title SEQ-07 Purchase
actor Reader
participant Storefront
participant Commerce
participant Provider
participant Entitlements
Reader -> Storefront: Start checkout
Storefront -> Commerce: Create order with idempotency key
Commerce -> Provider: Request hosted payment
Provider --> Commerce: Signed payment event
Commerce -> Commerce: Verify signature, amount, currency, event key
alt verified and eligible
 Commerce -> Entitlements: Grant once for purchased product
 Entitlements --> Reader: Available in library
else failed or uncertain
 Commerce --> Reader: Failure or pending; do not pay again yet
end
legend right
Solid arrow = request; dashed arrow = response.
Authorization, audit and error handling are required at each relevant boundary.
endlegend
@enduml

@startuml
' SEQ-08 Webhook and refund; scope: workflow interaction; FR-COM-001, FR-FIN-001. SOURCE NOT RENDER-VALIDATED.
title SEQ-08 Webhook and refund
participant Provider
participant Webhook
participant Ledger
participant Finance
Provider -> Webhook: Signed sale or refund event
Webhook -> Webhook: Verify signature and unique event key
alt valid new event
 Webhook -> Ledger: Post balanced entry or linked compensation
 Ledger --> Finance: Reconciliation record
else duplicate or invalid
 Webhook --> Provider: Acknowledge duplicate or reject invalid
end
Finance -> Provider: Reconcile ambiguous settlement before retry
legend right
Solid arrow = request; dashed arrow = response.
Authorization, audit and error handling are required at each relevant boundary.
endlegend
@enduml

@startuml
' SEQ-09 Royalty and payout; scope: workflow interaction; FR-FIN-001. SOURCE NOT RENDER-VALIDATED.
title SEQ-09 Royalty and payout
participant Sale
participant Royalty
participant Ledger
actor Finance
participant Provider
Sale -> Royalty: Verified sale and rule version
Royalty -> Ledger: Balanced attributable royalty posting once
Finance -> Ledger: Review cleared payable and holds
alt approved and amount within balance
 Finance -> Provider: Initiate idempotent payout
 Provider --> Finance: Status or uncertainty
 Finance -> Ledger: Reconcile and record outcome
else insufficient funds or dispute
 Ledger --> Finance: Block and record reason
end
legend right
Solid arrow = request; dashed arrow = response.
Authorization, audit and error handling are required at each relevant boundary.
endlegend
@enduml

